# AI Board NAT Controller — DNAT configuration v0.4.0 (development)
# Enabled|PublicIP|SourceIP|Protocol|ExternalPort|InternalIP|InternalPort
# Enabled: 1 enabled, 0 disabled (still syntax-checked).
# PublicIP: WAN_IP or explicit IPv4; ISP routing/ownership not verified.
# SourceIP: any, IPv4 or network-aligned IPv4 CIDR.
# Protocol: tcp, udp, both (expands TCP then UDP for each port entry).
# ExternalPort: 1–65535, inclusive colon range, or comma-separated list
# of ports/ranges (maximum 256 entries per line).
# InternalIP: single IPv4 host; must pass destination route validation.
# InternalPort: same (preserve port) or one numeric port for a single
# external port only. No port translation of lists or ranges.
# All fields mandatory, no whitespace, no inline comments or leading
# zeroes in numeric fields. Blank lines and full-line comments allowed.
# Enabled rules retain file order; overlapping public IP/protocol/port/
# source networks are rejected. Disjoint source networks may coexist.
# Maximum 4096 expanded enabled rules; invalid file emits no rules.
# Disabled rules do not reserve endpoints. Replace atomically with mv.
# Native forwarding takes precedence; no filter modifications planned.
# No hairpin or IPv6 support. All examples disabled. Parser only: do not
# deploy generated rules manually. Live engine still v0.3.0.
